# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
# Anything here can end up in an image layer, and a layer is readable by anyone
# who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Tests are not run inside the runtime image, and docs/ is git-ignored anyway.
tests/
docs/
data/

# Development scripts stay out -- except the one a deployment runs as its
# container command. Excluding the directory wholesale made `COPY scripts/`
# fail with "no source files were found", which is an eleven-second build
# failure that says nothing about .dockerignore being the reason.
scripts/
!scripts/serve-with-worker.sh

# The web client builds in its own image, from ./apps/web as its own context.
# Excluding it here keeps the React source out of the Python image entirely
# rather than merely out of the way -- the API has no use for it, and every
# file in an image is a file somebody has to account for.
apps/web

*.md
!README.md
